---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactForm from '../../components/ContactForm.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About | Liquid Zoo"
  description="MacAdmin and Client Platform Engineer based in Boston, MA. The story behind Liquid Zoo — plus a working resume."
>
  <main class="page about">
    <section class="section about-hero">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-label">// About</span>
        <h1 class="section-title">Hey 👋 My name is Andrew</h1>
      </div>
      <img
        class="about-header"
        src="/assets/img/about-header.webp"
        alt=""
        loading="eager"
      />

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          All my friends and family call me <strong>Spesh</strong>.
          I'm a MacAdmin, coder, music nerd, and gamer living in the greater
          Boston, MA area. By day I'm a Client Platform Engineer working on
          Apple fleet infrastructure; on the side I maintain a few open-source
          tools for the MacAdmin community.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="callout">
        <span class="callout-label">A note on names</span>
        <p>
          I'm in the process of taking my wife's last name. <strong>Speciale</strong>
          is my legal last name today, but professionally I go by
          <strong>Lerman</strong> — soon to be my legal name as well. If you
          find me as <em>Andrew Lerman</em> on GitHub, MacAdmins Slack, or
          LinkedIn, that's me. Either way, just call me Spesh.
        </p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <Section label='// Why "Liquid Zoo"?' class="about-section">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The name is a personal nod to a fond memory of mine — visiting the
          Atlanta Aquarium during my Apple Genius training years ago. Someone
          joked that aquariums are like "liquid zoos," and the name just
          stuck. It resonated even more as a metaphor for my wide range of
          interests: technology, music, gaming, software engineering,
          scripting languages (Python, shell, Swift), and some web
          development.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>The Zoo</strong> represents organized chaos — a collection
          of passions all living under one roof.
        </p>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section label="// Life outside tech" class="about-section">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>When I'm not coding or managing Mac fleets, you can likely find me:</p>
        <ul class="about-bullets">
          <li>🏠 Hanging out with my wife and family</li>
          <li>
            🎮 Deep in a single-player video game like
            <em>The Last of Us</em> (1 or 2), <em>Ghost of Tsushima</em>,
            <em>God of War</em>, or any of the <em>Spider-Man</em> games for PS5
          </li>
          <li>🎃 Watching horror movies (Halloween is a sacred holiday in our house)</li>
          <li>🎧 Producing music or listening to podcasts</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section label="// Daily tools" class="about-section">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The apps and utilities I lean on regularly — from development to
          device management to writing documentation. If you're a fellow
          MacAdmin, developer, or automation nerd, you might find a few
          favorites here.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="daily-tools">
        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>💻 Hardware</h4>
          <p>
            All my development happens on a
            <a href="https://www.apple.com/macbook-pro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MacBook Pro (M1 Max)</a>
            with 32&nbsp;GB RAM, paired with a Samsung ViewFinity S949 49"
            ultrawide.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.keychron.com/products/keychron-k10-pro-qmk-via-wireless-mechanical-keyboard" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Keychron K10 Pro</a>
              keyboard
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.logitech.com/en-us/shop/p/mx-master-3s-mac-bluetooth-mouse.910-006570" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Logitech MX Master 3S</a>
              mouse
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.apple.com/airpods-max/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AirPods Max</a>
              for blocking out the world
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>🧑‍💻 Development</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Visual Studio Code</a>
              and
              <a href="https://jetbrains.com/pycharm/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PyCharm CE</a>
              — IDEs of choice for Python, scripting, and web work
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.warp.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Warp</a>
              — terminal client, running
              <a href="https://ohmyz.sh" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oh My Zsh</a>
              with the
              <a href="https://github.com/zsh-users/zsh-syntax-highlighting" target="_blank" rel="noopener">zsh-syntax-highlighting</a>
              plugin
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>🌐 API testing &amp; browsers</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://altairgraphql.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Altair GraphQL Client</a>
              — primarily for the Jamf Protect API
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.postman.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Postman</a>
              — a classic for testing REST APIs
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://arc.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Arc</a>,
              <a href="https://www.google.com/chrome/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chrome</a>, and
              <a href="https://www.apple.com/safari/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Safari</a>
              — yes, I rotate between all three 🙃
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>📝 Notes &amp; docs</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.notion.so/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Notion</a>
              — my second brain: documentation, SOPs, blog drafts, task management
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>🔒 MacAdmin utilities</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.mothersruin.com/software/Apparency/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apparency</a>
              — code-signing info and application inspection
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://www.mothersruin.com/software/SuspiciousPackage/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Suspicious Package</a>
              — preview <code>.pkg</code> installer contents before running
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="daily-tools-group">
          <h4>🔧 Workflow helpers</h4>
          <ul>
            <li>
              <a href="https://copyless.net/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CopyLess 2</a>
              — clipboard manager with history and favorites
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://rectangleapp.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rectangle Pro</a>
              — window management with keyboard shortcuts
            </li>
            <li>
              <a href="https://textexpander.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TextExpander</a>
              — snippet/expansion tool for faster typing
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section label="// Experience" class="resume-section">
      <div class="resume-roles">
        <article class="resume-role">
          <header class="resume-role-head">
            <div>
              <h3 class="resume-role-title">Client Platform Engineer</h3>
            </div>
            <span class="resume-role-meta">Current</span>
          </header>
          <ul class="resume-bullets">
            <li>Designed and led implementation of a full Infrastructure-as-Code pipeline for macOS MDM, aligning platform engineering and security around version-controlled, auditable deployments.</li>
            <li>Built a Slack-based deployment system for Jamf App Installers, partnering with end users to refine notification behavior and improve adoption of update workflows.</li>
            <li>Developed a real-time patch management dashboard integrating Jamf and CrowdStrike APIs, enabling security and IT to identify and respond to vulnerable endpoints faster.</li>
            <li>Led migration from SimpleMDM to Jamf Pro with automated cleanup and communication workflows.</li>
            <li>Collaborated with Security and Engineering on supply-chain security initiatives.</li>
            <li>Expanded endpoint management to Windows environments via Microsoft Graph API, PowerShell, and GitHub Actions.</li>
            <li>Built and open-sourced a Jamf MCP server, contributing to the broader MacAdmin community.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-role">
          <header class="resume-role-head">
            <div>
              <h3 class="resume-role-title">Internal Systems Administrator II</h3>
            </div>
            <span class="resume-role-meta">Prior</span>
          </header>
          <ul class="resume-bullets">
            <li>Championed the expansion of macOS adoption in a Windows-dominant environment, enabling a company-wide choice program.</li>
            <li>Designed internal automation tools — desktop onboarding app, CLI troubleshooting suite — to improve consistency and reduce manual support load.</li>
            <li>Integrated Jamf Pro with Apple Business Manager for fully automated device enrollment.</li>
            <li>Implemented Jamf Protect with Security Operations to improve endpoint compliance and threat visibility.</li>
            <li>Built a Slack-integrated diagnostics API that gave L1 support real-time system insights.</li>
            <li>Enforced CVE-aligned patching policies via CrowdStrike Falcon detections.</li>
            <li>Operationalized open-source tools (Nudge, Setup Your Mac) for compliance with a friendly user experience.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="resume-role">
          <header class="resume-role-head">
            <div>
              <h3 class="resume-role-title">Genius · Lead Trainer · Online Store Manager</h3>
              <p class="resume-role-company">Apple Inc. · Multiple Locations, MA</p>
            </div>
            <span class="resume-role-meta">2010 — 2022</span>
          </header>
          <ul class="resume-bullets">
            <li>Certified hardware and software repair technician; maintained a 94/100 team member satisfaction score during peak escalation periods.</li>
            <li>Designed and led onboarding programs for 60+ new and seasonal employees across New England as Lead Trainer.</li>
            <li>Managed escalated support cases for Apple's online store using SAP tools.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <Section label="// Technical skills" class="resume-section">
      <div class="resume-skills">
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Apple Ecosystem</h4>
          <p>macOS, iOS, iPadOS, Apple Business Manager, DEP</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Device Management</h4>
          <p>Jamf Pro, Jamf Protect, Jamf Connect, SimpleMDM, Fleet</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Infrastructure &amp; Automation</h4>
          <p>Terraform, GitHub Actions, CI/CD, Workato, Okta Workflows</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Scripting &amp; Development</h4>
          <p>Python, Bash/zsh, Swift, JavaScript/TypeScript, REST APIs, Git</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Security &amp; Compliance</h4>
          <p>CrowdStrike Falcon, FileVault, OSQuery, Kolide, Koi</p>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-skill-group">
          <h4>Identity &amp; Access</h4>
          <p>Okta, Microsoft Entra ID, Google Workspace, ConductorOne, SailPoint</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Section>

    <section class="section resume-section resume-two-col">
      <div class="resume-two-col-cell">
        <span class="section-label">// Open source</span>
        <h2 class="sr-only">Open source</h2>
        <ul class="resume-projects">
          <li>
            <strong>Patcher</strong> — Patch reporting for Jamf-managed fleets ·
            <a href="https://github.com/liquidz00/Patcher" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> ·
            <a href="https://patcher.readthedocs.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>JamfMCP</strong> — MCP server for Jamf Pro ·
            <a href="https://github.com/liquidz00/JamfMCP" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> ·
            <a href="https://jamfmcp.readthedocs.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>pymdm</strong> — Python toolkit for MDM workflows ·
            <a href="https://github.com/liquidz00/pymdm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> ·
            <a href="https://pymdm.readthedocs.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Docs</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>More on the <a href="/projects/">projects page</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="resume-two-col-cell">
        <span class="section-label">// Certifications</span>
        <h2 class="sr-only">Certifications</h2>
        <div class="cert-grid">
          <div class="cert-tag">Jamf 400 · Certified Expert</div>
          <div class="cert-tag">Jamf 370 · Endpoint Security Admin</div>
          <div class="cert-tag">Jamf 300 · Certified Admin</div>
          <div class="cert-tag">Jamf 200 · Certified Technician</div>
          <div class="cert-tag">ACMT · Apple Certified Mac Technician</div>
          <div class="cert-tag">ACiT · Apple Certified iOS Technician</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Section label="// Get in touch" class="about-section">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The fastest way to reach me is a DM on the
          <a href="https://www.macadmins.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MacAdmins Slack</a>
          — I'm there as <strong>@liquidzoo</strong>. You can also find me on
          <a href="https://github.com/liquidz00" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>,
          <a href="https://community.jamf.com/t5/user/viewprofilepage/user-id/140536" target="_blank" rel="noopener">JamfNation</a>,
          or
          <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/andrewspeciale" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Need a copy of my resume? <strong>Reach out via Slack or LinkedIn</strong> and I'll send the PDF over.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prefer not to use any of the above? Drop a note here:
        </p>
      </div>

      <ContactForm />
    </Section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
